1. Commercialization, Monetization, and the Roadmap

Terminal Buddy’s commercial strategy is built on the principle of "Personalization without Complexity." This is realized through the "Creator Corner" and a template-driven network effect.

The Creator Corner: A Network Effect Engine

User-generated templates (custom fonts, colors, and layout presets) are more than just customizations; they are a Network Effect engine. Customization acts as Retention (switching cost), while sharing these templates on the "Hub" serves as Viral Marketing. As users share setups like "Dyslexia-Friendly Dark" or "ADHD Focus Mode," they effectively market the product to niche, high-value communities.

Monetization Tiers

Monetization follows an Open Core model. Hard Requirement: Core accessibility features are never gated behind a paywall.

